# Worker storage root is /app == ./backend (bind mount). The Prefect process
# worker copies this whole tree into a fresh temp dir for EVERY flow run. With
# an empty ignore it copies backend/.venv (~1.8 GB of ML wheels: torch,
# transformers, lightgbm, …) plus caches, so runs stall for minutes at
# "Downloading flow code from storage at '/app'" and pile up. The worker has its
# own installed environment — only the pfip package + schedules are needed to
# import and run the flows. Exclude everything heavy below.

# The big one: the host virtualenv (not used by the worker, which has its own).
.venv/
venv/
env/

# Python caches / build / test artifacts
**/__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/
build/
dist/
*.egg-info/

# ML run artifacts
mlruns/
mlartifacts/

# Secrets / sessions / logs (never copy into worker temp dirs)
.env
*.session
*.log
